.nh
.TH "GYRO" "1" "Nov 2026" "Gyro Hosting" "gyro manual"

.SH NAME
gyro-container-logs - Search and follow the logs of an environment or one service


.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBgyro container logs  [SERVICE] [flags]\fP


.SH DESCRIPTION
Shows what your containers wrote to stdout / stderr, oldest first. Without a service every service of the
environment is searched. Filters: --filter (line contains, case-insensitive), --exclude, --level (error|warn|info|debug)
and --where field conditions on JSON / logfmt lines (status>=500, method=POST, path~/api; repeat the flag for more).
--follow keeps printing new lines (polls every 2 s, Ctrl-C stops). --all pages back through the whole window
(up to 100,000 lines). How far back you can go depends on the log package (free: 7 days; gyro container log-usage).


.SH OPTIONS
\fB--all\fP[=false]
	page back through the whole window (max 100,000 lines)

.PP
\fB--end\fP=""
	end time (RFC3339 or a duration ago)

.PP
\fB--exclude\fP=""
	line does not contain this text

.PP
\fB--filter\fP=""
	line contains this text (case-insensitive)

.PP
\fB-f\fP, \fB--follow\fP[=false]
	keep printing new lines (Ctrl-C stops)

.PP
\fB-h\fP, \fB--help\fP[=false]
	help for logs

.PP
\fB--level\fP=""
	error | warn | info | debug

.PP
\fB--limit\fP=0
	lines per page (default 300, max 5000)

.PP
\fB--parse\fP=""
	json | logfmt

.PP
\fB--previous\fP[=false]
	output of the last crashed replica of the service

.PP
\fB--service\fP=""
	only this service (same as the second argument)

.PP
\fB--since\fP=""
	window ending now: 30m, 6h, 7d (default 1h; 15m with --follow)

.PP
\fB--start\fP=""
	start time (RFC3339 or a duration ago, e.g. 3d); one query spans at most 31 days

.PP
\fB--where\fP=[]
	field condition on JSON / logfmt lines: status>=500, method=POST, path~/api (repeatable)


.SH OPTIONS INHERITED FROM PARENT COMMANDS
\fB--account\fP=""
	act in another account you are a panel user of (id from \fBgyro account list\fR; "self" = your own; env GYRO_ACCOUNT, profile default: \fBgyro account use\fR)

.PP
\fB--api-url\fP=""
	API base URL (env GYRO_API_URL)

.PP
\fB--debug\fP[=false]
	log HTTP requests to stderr (secrets masked)

.PP
\fB--lang\fP=""
	message language: tr or en (default from locale)

.PP
\fB--no-color\fP[=false]
	disable colours (also NO_COLOR)

.PP
\fB--no-header\fP[=false]
	omit the table header

.PP
\fB-o\fP, \fB--output\fP=""
	output format: table, json, yaml, text

.PP
\fB-p\fP, \fB--profile\fP=""
	profile to use (env GYRO_PROFILE)

.PP
\fB--query\fP=""
	JMESPath query applied to the result

.PP
\fB-q\fP, \fB--quiet\fP[=false]
	print only ids

.PP
\fB--timeout\fP=0s
	overall timeout, e.g. 30s, 10m

.PP
\fB--wide\fP[=false]
	show all table columns

.PP
\fB-y\fP, \fB--yes\fP[=false]
	do not ask for confirmation


.SH EXAMPLE
.EX
  gyro container logs 17000 api --since 30m
  gyro container logs 17000 --level error --since 24h
  gyro container logs 17000 api --where 'status>=500' --where 'path~/api' --since 2h
  gyro container logs 17000 api -f
.EE


.SH SEE ALSO
\fBgyro-container(1)\fP
